WEBVTT

00:00:01.241 --> 00:00:02.741
[PHOENIX] While the Kurain Urn
was being stolen,

00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:05.575
a brutal murder took place in
the office of Kane Bullard,

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:07.700
CEO of KB Security.

00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:10.908
Since Ron's alibi for the theft
put him in that very office,

00:00:10.991 --> 00:00:13.450
he was arrested
once more for murder.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.116
But the actual
assassin was someone

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.158
artfully arranging all this
from behind the backdrop.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.658
This court is hereby
in session for the murder trial

00:00:27.741 --> 00:00:29.450
of Mister Ron DeLite.

00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:30.575
[RON whimpers]

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.283
Court is now
in session for the trial

00:00:38.366 --> 00:00:40.575
of Luke Atmey.
Please take your seats.

00:00:40.658 --> 00:00:43.033
[PHOENIX]
Two trials linked at the core.

00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:44.741
I have to get him to the stand.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.908
If the prosecution is ready.

00:02:18.991 --> 00:02:20.408
You may now proceed.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.991
I always limit myself
to no more than 17 cups

00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:26.491
of coffee during
any given trial.

00:02:26.575 --> 00:02:28.741
But that first one
is something special.

00:02:28.825 --> 00:02:30.783
Gives me the right
amount of stimulation.

00:02:32.158 --> 00:02:33.866
[JUDGE]
Uh. Okay.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.325
[PHOENIX] I get the feeling
he's ready to grind me up.

00:02:37.408 --> 00:02:38.658
[GODOT]
I did some digging.

00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:40.950
Trying to find out exactly
why you were terminated

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.450
from KB security last year.

00:02:43.533 --> 00:02:44.533
[RON whimpers]

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.075
It was because
of your wife, wasn't it?

00:02:48.158 --> 00:02:49.116
Because of me?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.241
[BOTH gasp]

00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:52.658
[RON gasps]
No. You got it all wrong.

00:02:52.741 --> 00:02:54.075
Is that so?

00:02:54.158 --> 00:02:56.575
In order to satisfy her
thirst for spending,

00:02:56.658 --> 00:02:59.991
you stole confidential company
data you thought you could sell.

00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:02.741
The CEO found out and
poured you down the drain.

00:03:02.825 --> 00:03:04.200
[RON grunts]

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.575
[GODOT] Of course, the truth
would leave a bitter taste

00:03:05.658 --> 00:03:07.116
in the missus' mouth.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.950
Quitting on "principle"
sounds much sweeter.

00:03:11.116 --> 00:03:12.950
Personally,
I'd call it saccharine.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.658
[RON whimpers]

00:03:14.741 --> 00:03:16.533
Mister Bullard then
brewed up a plan to spill

00:03:16.616 --> 00:03:17.991
the beans about you.

00:03:18.075 --> 00:03:21.075
Blackmail. You decided
he needed to get burned.

00:03:22.658 --> 00:03:25.033
Ronnie. That can't be true...

00:03:25.116 --> 00:03:26.241
[RON whimpers]

00:03:26.325 --> 00:03:28.950
Definitely a robust
motive if you ask me.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.616
This is bad.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.200
[GODOT] Moving on. What did you
do after receiving this letter?

00:03:35.283 --> 00:03:36.741
We need to know.

00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:39.491
[RON gasps]
Just what it said.

00:03:39.575 --> 00:03:41.450
I followed the letter's
instructions and went up

00:03:41.533 --> 00:03:43.658
to my old boss's office.

00:03:43.741 --> 00:03:44.908
I opened the door...

00:03:46.366 --> 00:03:48.616
[RON] ...and that's when
I saw a suspicious shadow!

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:55.158
They clocked me hard on the
forehead and knocked me out.

00:03:55.241 --> 00:03:58.283
Next thing I knew,
Bullard was dead on the floor!

00:03:58.366 --> 00:03:59.783
[gasps]

00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:02.075
[BOTH whimper]

00:04:02.158 --> 00:04:05.241
[gasps] If I hadn't decided
to wear it that night,

00:04:05.325 --> 00:04:07.116
I might have died
right there beside him.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.116
[GODOT]
Huh?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.575
Wait, what protected you?

00:04:09.658 --> 00:04:11.325
Oh, I was wearing my mask.

00:04:11.408 --> 00:04:12.908
So, you wore a costume?

00:04:12.991 --> 00:04:15.491
Yeah. I was wearing
my full "Phantom Thief"

00:04:15.575 --> 00:04:17.866
regalia for the meeting.
Mask and all.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.200
[JUDGE gasps]

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.658
[gasping]

00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:24.700
Uh. Is that important?

00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:26.700
Guess I didn't think
to mention it earlier.

00:04:26.783 --> 00:04:28.533
It is kind of a major detail.

00:04:28.616 --> 00:04:31.158
I would've really
liked to have known that.

00:04:32.241 --> 00:04:34.033
Since I was being
blackmailed over my identity

00:04:34.116 --> 00:04:36.408
as Mask DeMasque,
seemed like showing up

00:04:36.491 --> 00:04:38.825
in the costume would be
the thing to do, yeah?

00:04:38.908 --> 00:04:40.325
[groans]

00:04:40.408 --> 00:04:42.575
I gotta start to
move things along.

00:04:42.658 --> 00:04:46.283
[PAYNE chuckles] Do you have
anything to add, Mr. Atmey?

00:04:46.366 --> 00:04:50.533
[LUKE chuckles] Perfect
performance Prosecutor Payne.

00:04:50.616 --> 00:04:53.950
Your professionalism
is without parallel.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.075
It appears that we're
absolutely accelerating

00:04:56.158 --> 00:04:58.825
toward appropriate adjudication.

00:04:58.908 --> 00:05:00.491
As far as stories go,

00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:03.533
I'm finding the kid's
testimony a bit unpalatable.

00:05:03.616 --> 00:05:05.908
He walked in and
was knocked out cold?

00:05:05.991 --> 00:05:07.866
Bit hard for me to swallow.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.408
Look at the evidence!

00:05:09.491 --> 00:05:12.033
There are logs documenting
every time the emergency buzzer

00:05:12.116 --> 00:05:13.908
in that office rang up security.

00:05:13.991 --> 00:05:15.616
And according to the records,

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.325
the alarm was hit
just after 1 AM.

00:05:18.408 --> 00:05:19.408
If Ron were the killer,

00:05:19.491 --> 00:05:21.200
he would've run
as soon as it sounded.

00:05:21.283 --> 00:05:22.450
You sure of that?

00:05:22.533 --> 00:05:24.658
He would know a
security guard was on the way.

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:26.991
But Ron's previous testimony
stated that he hid

00:05:27.075 --> 00:05:29.950
Mister Bullard's body in
the safe after he came to.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.783
Would a killer stay
at the scene when he assumed

00:05:31.866 --> 00:05:32.866
a guard was on the way?

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.491
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:05:34.575 --> 00:05:36.408
But the fact of the matter
is the security guard

00:05:36.491 --> 00:05:37.866
never arrived to the scene.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.575
Ah. Yeah, well.
That's just a coincidence.

00:05:41.658 --> 00:05:42.991
[BUTZ giggles]

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:45.158
Perhaps the watchman on
duty at the time simply didn't

00:05:45.241 --> 00:05:46.783
notice the buzzer going off?

00:05:46.866 --> 00:05:48.283
[PHOENIX]
Not a chance.

00:05:48.366 --> 00:05:51.450
The alarm is ear-splittingly
loud and impossible to miss.

00:05:51.533 --> 00:05:54.866
That is... Unless, you
were completely unconscious

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.200
when it sounded, of course.

00:05:56.283 --> 00:05:58.116
[JUDGE] You mean the
guard was unconscious?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.866
Surely, you do recall
the defendant's testimony?

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.908
Someone hit him over the
head and he only discovered

00:06:02.991 --> 00:06:04.991
the victim's body
when he woke up.

00:06:05.075 --> 00:06:06.283
So what are you trying to say?

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.950
Obviously, when
the alarm went off,

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.533
Ron DeLite was
passed out on the floor.

00:06:11.616 --> 00:06:13.783
He was? Right then?

00:06:13.866 --> 00:06:15.575
By the time the buzzer rang,

00:06:15.658 --> 00:06:18.158
Kane Bullard had already
been brutally murdered,

00:06:18.241 --> 00:06:20.241
and the defendant was
attacked and rendered

00:06:20.325 --> 00:06:22.741
completely unconscious.

00:06:22.825 --> 00:06:25.616
With the real killer
choosing that window to escape.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.408
What conclusion
would be reached?

00:06:27.491 --> 00:06:29.491
[RON] Anybody walking into
that situation would think

00:06:29.575 --> 00:06:31.491
I was the murderer!

00:06:31.575 --> 00:06:35.366
And so! The emergency buzzer was
set off by the actual killer!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.991
It was all an attempt
to make Ron DeLite look guilty--

00:06:38.075 --> 00:06:38.991
to frame him!

00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:40.241
[GODOT grunts]

00:06:43.741 --> 00:06:45.991
And just who might
this "actual killer" be?

00:06:46.075 --> 00:06:48.658
Are you prepared to
make an accusation?

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.575
I believe that it's Luke Atmey.

00:06:51.658 --> 00:06:53.033
Oh, yeah?

00:06:53.116 --> 00:06:55.783
You do realize the phantom
thief is currently on trial.

00:06:55.866 --> 00:06:58.325
Just one courtroom
over, in fact.

00:06:58.408 --> 00:07:00.991
[PHOENIX]
He's not the phantom thief.

00:07:01.075 --> 00:07:03.783
Two crimes were being
committed simultaneously.

00:07:03.866 --> 00:07:06.116
One theft and one murder.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.866
Which of those would
be the lesser offense?

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:12.200
[JUDGE] No question, it would
clearly be the robbery.

00:07:12.283 --> 00:07:14.991
If the robbery charge
resulted in a conviction,

00:07:15.075 --> 00:07:17.866
that could be used as
an alibi for the murder.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.075
The trial next door
is a cover-up!

00:07:20.158 --> 00:07:23.450
A cunning scheme deviously
devised by Luke Atmey!

00:07:23.533 --> 00:07:25.825
--[JUDGE] Hmm?
--You can't be serious.

00:07:25.908 --> 00:07:28.700
The defense requests
that Luke Atmey take the stand!

00:07:28.783 --> 00:07:32.533
Right now! Before the
guilty verdict is declared!

00:07:38.283 --> 00:07:40.700
[JUDGE] Now then, this court
is once again in session.

00:07:40.783 --> 00:07:43.075
[LUKE growls]

00:07:43.158 --> 00:07:44.950
Well, he's here, so now what?

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.700
Things are about to get real.

00:07:47.783 --> 00:07:50.408
At 1 AM, the night
of September 12th,

00:07:50.491 --> 00:07:53.700
Kane Bullard was killed in
his office at KB security.

00:07:53.783 --> 00:07:55.950
What were you
doing at that time?

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:59.366
You insist upon the same
imbecilic inquiry, is that it?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.491
I had made a particular pledge.

00:08:01.575 --> 00:08:03.241
Yes. To purloin a
priceless piece,

00:08:03.325 --> 00:08:05.241
and was in the process
of perpetration.

00:08:05.325 --> 00:08:07.366
Simply scrutinize the
stamp on the surveillance

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.741
to substantiate said statement
signaling the specific second.

00:08:14.158 --> 00:08:15.116
[gasps]

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.450
At that time,
you were actually in

00:08:16.533 --> 00:08:19.491
the CEO's office at KB Security.

00:08:19.575 --> 00:08:21.658
There is no way this
picture could've been taken

00:08:21.741 --> 00:08:22.866
when you claim.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:24.075
[LUKE]
Nonsense!

00:08:24.158 --> 00:08:26.200
[JUDGE]
Care to elaborate, Mr. Wright?

00:08:26.283 --> 00:08:28.241
What I'm saying is,
this photograph was taken

00:08:28.325 --> 00:08:31.991
at 1 AM, several days before
the dual crimes were committed.

00:08:32.075 --> 00:08:35.158
You're alleging this
photo was staged, somehow?

00:08:35.241 --> 00:08:37.075
[PHOENIX] Yes. And on
the night in question,

00:08:37.158 --> 00:08:40.950
you made sure to kill Kane
Bullard at the exact same time.

00:08:41.033 --> 00:08:42.200
And this photo...

00:08:42.283 --> 00:08:44.200
...is nothing but a false alibi!

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.033
Argh! Stop that!

00:08:47.116 --> 00:08:49.325
The stamp shows
time but not date,

00:08:49.408 --> 00:08:50.866
you used that to your advantage.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:52.658
[GODOT]
Objection!

00:08:52.741 --> 00:08:57.241
Quite an unsavory accusation.
But there's not a drop of proof.

00:08:57.325 --> 00:09:00.241
[PHOENIX] Hm. On the contrary,
there is considerably more

00:09:00.325 --> 00:09:01.741
than just a drop.

00:09:01.825 --> 00:09:04.450
But what may be more damning
is what's missing entirely.

00:09:04.533 --> 00:09:05.616
[LUKE]
Huh?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.491
[PHOENIX]
The golden statue of Ami Fey.

00:09:07.575 --> 00:09:09.158
In fact, the exhibit's
coordinator made

00:09:09.241 --> 00:09:10.658
a statement about it.

00:09:10.741 --> 00:09:11.950
[ANDREWS] With the
urn back in one piece,

00:09:12.033 --> 00:09:14.908
I realized how ugly
the paint stains looked.

00:09:14.991 --> 00:09:18.325
So I hid them
behind Mystic Ami's statue.

00:09:18.408 --> 00:09:19.700
On the night in question,

00:09:19.783 --> 00:09:22.408
the statue was in direct
view of the security camera.

00:09:22.491 --> 00:09:24.158
But then somebody
pushed it away.

00:09:24.241 --> 00:09:27.325
I'm sure it was you,
Detective Luke Atmey.

00:09:27.408 --> 00:09:28.741
[LUKE growls]

00:09:28.825 --> 00:09:31.075
Care to share a motive for that?

00:09:31.158 --> 00:09:32.658
[PHOENIX]
Continuity.

00:09:32.741 --> 00:09:34.783
If you recall when the statue
was delivered to the warehouse,

00:09:34.866 --> 00:09:36.366
it makes perfect sense.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.325
It arrived there
the day before the crimes.

00:09:39.408 --> 00:09:41.200
Wait. Hold the phone.

00:09:41.283 --> 00:09:42.700
You see now?

00:09:42.783 --> 00:09:45.283
That's why I'm confident this
photo was taken days prior

00:09:45.366 --> 00:09:46.825
to the incidents.

00:09:46.908 --> 00:09:50.283
When that golden
statue wasn't in the frame.

00:09:50.366 --> 00:09:52.991
It must've been pretty
jarring walking into the scene.

00:09:53.075 --> 00:09:55.325
Suddenly there was a large
set-piece right in the shot,

00:09:55.408 --> 00:09:57.116
where it hadn't been before.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.908
Which means, at the very least,

00:09:58.991 --> 00:10:01.450
you had to move it somewhere
out of the line of sight.

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:03.491
So everything would
match your pictorial alibi

00:10:03.575 --> 00:10:05.533
for Bullard's murder.

00:10:05.616 --> 00:10:07.825
Lordly Tailor provided
the security camera,

00:10:07.908 --> 00:10:10.200
which prevented you from
tampering with the photo.

00:10:10.283 --> 00:10:12.283
But you knew that
no date would be shown,

00:10:12.366 --> 00:10:14.866
and exploited that fact!

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:16.908
I'm right! Aren't I?

00:10:16.991 --> 00:10:18.075
Answer me!

00:10:18.158 --> 00:10:20.908
Agh, gwah!

00:10:20.991 --> 00:10:22.866
[GODOT]
This is cup 11.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.991
I'm still good till the
last nutty drop of the 17th.

00:10:26.075 --> 00:10:29.325
So you allege Detective Atmey
brewed this whole thing up?

00:10:29.408 --> 00:10:30.575
[PHOENIX]
I do.

00:10:30.658 --> 00:10:33.616
[GODOT] Hmph.
That just won't fly, mi amigo.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:34.950
Oh, yeah?

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:37.158
The question isn't where
he was several days before

00:10:37.241 --> 00:10:40.200
the crime, but at the time
it was being committed.

00:10:40.283 --> 00:10:42.450
You got a claim, but no proof.

00:10:42.533 --> 00:10:44.783
And kid, that's
worse than decaf.

00:10:44.866 --> 00:10:46.075
[PHOENIX growls]

00:10:46.158 --> 00:10:47.950
[CROWD murmurin

00:10:48.033 --> 00:10:51.283
Hey, Nick?
Can you prove where he was?

00:10:51.366 --> 00:10:52.741
What do we do?

00:10:53.658 --> 00:10:55.866
[BOTH gasp]

00:10:55.950 --> 00:11:00.116
My proof? I don't know.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.700
[GODOT]
There we are!

00:11:01.783 --> 00:11:04.075
Then I say it's about time for
the phantom thief to head back

00:11:04.158 --> 00:11:07.825
to his own trial and get served
a hot cuppa justice juice.

00:11:07.908 --> 00:11:09.575
One venti verdict, please.

00:11:09.658 --> 00:11:10.866
No! Not yet!

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.950
[LUKE chuckles, cackles]

00:11:16.033 --> 00:11:18.408
Zvarri. I am both
the virtuous and valorous

00:11:18.491 --> 00:11:20.866
investigator, and the
vainglorious villain,

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.366
which will be verified by my
verdict in the very next room.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.825
I am a vessel of veracity.

00:11:25.908 --> 00:11:28.575
And the truth of this twisted
transgression is that Ron DeLite

00:11:28.658 --> 00:11:30.533
is the taker of life.

00:11:30.616 --> 00:11:32.658
The fact that foppish
fool is a phantom thief

00:11:32.741 --> 00:11:34.866
fanatic is merely
a fortuitous fluke.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.991
I mean, this man here
is such a massive maven

00:11:37.075 --> 00:11:38.491
of Mask DeMasque,

00:11:38.575 --> 00:11:40.450
that he was moved to masquerade
as the mythical midnighter

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.616
when meeting his blackmailer.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.491
As the highwayman himself,
his homage is humbling.

00:11:45.575 --> 00:11:47.783
[cackles]

00:11:47.866 --> 00:11:50.241
No. Ron's gonna
get fried for this.

00:11:50.325 --> 00:11:51.950
We can't give up now!

00:11:52.033 --> 00:11:53.616
If we find the evidence
we need, then--

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.783
We don't have that kind of time.

00:11:55.866 --> 00:11:57.158
But why not?

00:11:57.241 --> 00:11:59.741
Because of a little
thing we call double jeopardy.

00:11:59.825 --> 00:12:00.908
Huh?

00:12:00.991 --> 00:12:02.116
That means if a
defendant has been brought

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.241
to trial and declared
innocent in a case,

00:12:05.325 --> 00:12:07.450
then it's impossible for
them to stand trial again for

00:12:07.533 --> 00:12:09.491
the exact same offense.

00:12:09.575 --> 00:12:11.616
In the extremely likely
event he is roasted in

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.491
the next room and found guilty
for the Phantom Thief crime...

00:12:14.575 --> 00:12:16.450
...that would be
an airtight alibi.

00:12:16.533 --> 00:12:18.241
It would prove beyond
a shadow of a doubt

00:12:18.325 --> 00:12:20.533
his innocence in
Bullard's murder.

00:12:20.616 --> 00:12:22.700
If Mister Atmey was
proven to be elsewhere

00:12:22.783 --> 00:12:24.616
and found innocent of this
heinous crime, he could

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.241
never be tried for it again.

00:12:26.325 --> 00:12:27.908
Finally clear on it now?

00:12:27.991 --> 00:12:29.575
Poor Ron...

00:12:29.658 --> 00:12:31.158
[PHOENIX growls]

00:12:31.241 --> 00:12:34.741
[PHOENIX] What can I do? I can't
let this guy get away with it.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:36.991
[MIA]
Phoenix.

00:12:37.075 --> 00:12:38.241
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:12:38.325 --> 00:12:40.908
[MIA]
This is your moment to laugh.

00:12:40.991 --> 00:12:44.450
[CROWD murmurin]

00:12:44.533 --> 00:12:45.783
[MIA]
Come on, Phoenix.

00:12:45.866 --> 00:12:47.616
Look at this as an opportunity.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.700
It can't be. She's here?

00:12:50.783 --> 00:12:52.283
Turn your thinking around.

00:12:52.366 --> 00:12:53.450
You've got this.

00:12:53.533 --> 00:12:55.491
Don't you remember
what I used to tell you?

00:12:55.575 --> 00:12:57.533
When things seem
most desperate, we laugh.

00:12:57.616 --> 00:13:00.075
[PHOENIX]
Mia, I...

00:13:00.158 --> 00:13:02.950
We can talk later.
There's work to be done.

00:13:03.033 --> 00:13:06.450
But the cross-examination
is over now.

00:13:06.533 --> 00:13:08.200
It's not finished quite yet.

00:13:08.283 --> 00:13:11.033
That garrulous detective
ran his mouth too much.

00:13:11.116 --> 00:13:12.241
In what way?

00:13:12.325 --> 00:13:13.866
He got carried away
in what he was saying

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:15.658
and made a fatal mistake.

00:13:15.741 --> 00:13:16.741
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:13:16.825 --> 00:13:19.075
[MIA]
Think about what he just said.

00:13:19.158 --> 00:13:20.866
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.866
Gentlemen and gentlewomen.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.866
It's time for me
to face my fate.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.200
<i>Tout à l'heure.</i>

00:13:26.283 --> 00:13:28.033
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:13:28.116 --> 00:13:29.116
Wait. Come again?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.866
Luke Atmey.
You can't leave here.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.741
You basically confessed.

00:13:33.825 --> 00:13:35.991
By placing yourself at
the scene of the murder!

00:13:36.075 --> 00:13:37.241
Absurd!

00:13:37.325 --> 00:13:39.283
[PHOENIX] Recall what
you just told the court.

00:13:39.366 --> 00:13:41.283
I mean, this man here
is such a massive maven

00:13:41.366 --> 00:13:42.783
of Mask DeMasque,

00:13:42.866 --> 00:13:44.908
that he was moved to masquerade
as the mythical midnighter

00:13:44.991 --> 00:13:46.616
when meeting his blackmailer.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.241
I was simply stating a fact.

00:13:48.325 --> 00:13:51.575
[PHOENIX] How did you know
about that particular detail?

00:13:51.658 --> 00:13:53.450
I cannot comprehend your query.

00:13:53.533 --> 00:13:55.158
The DeMasque costume.

00:13:55.241 --> 00:13:57.491
Ron was indeed
wearing it on that night.

00:13:57.575 --> 00:14:00.116
But that specific fact was
not actually revealed until

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.283
earlier today in
this very courtroom.

00:14:02.366 --> 00:14:03.575
Is that important?

00:14:03.658 --> 00:14:05.408
Guess I didn't think
to mention it earlier.

00:14:05.491 --> 00:14:07.116
At the time
he shared that info with us,

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.033
you were standing trial
in another courtroom,

00:14:09.116 --> 00:14:10.991
so there's no way you
could have known about it.

00:14:11.075 --> 00:14:12.200
[gasps]

00:14:12.283 --> 00:14:13.950
[CROWD murmuring]

00:14:14.033 --> 00:14:16.325
But he obviously
did know that somehow.

00:14:16.408 --> 00:14:18.408
[PHOENIX] Mm-hmm. There's
only one explanation how

00:14:18.491 --> 00:14:20.825
he could corroborate
Ron's testimony.

00:14:20.908 --> 00:14:22.366
Earlier, Ron stated
that he had seen

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:25.325
a suspicious shadow just
before he was attacked.

00:14:25.408 --> 00:14:28.241
If you shift the perspective
and turn things around,

00:14:28.325 --> 00:14:31.450
that would also mean
the shadow saw Ron, as well.

00:14:35.325 --> 00:14:38.450
[PHOENIX] That's how Atmey knew
about the Mask DeMasque costume.

00:14:39.908 --> 00:14:42.241
[LUKE whimpers]

00:14:42.325 --> 00:14:44.866
Because, he was on the scene.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.033
Committing murder!

00:14:47.116 --> 00:14:49.825
[LUKE yells]

00:14:49.908 --> 00:14:51.366
[RON gasps]

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.575
[MIA]
Hmm.

00:14:52.658 --> 00:14:54.241
Now look, Atmey.

00:14:54.325 --> 00:14:57.158
You have to see how
you just fingered yourself.

00:14:57.241 --> 00:14:58.908
So confess to it!

00:14:58.991 --> 00:15:01.408
Bravo!

00:15:01.491 --> 00:15:04.616
That pyre in your peepers
and your cuspidated coiffure...

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:05.825
...counselor!

00:15:05.908 --> 00:15:09.158
You, sir... without
a dollop of doubt...

00:15:09.241 --> 00:15:12.658
...do deserve...
A downpour of distinction!

00:15:12.741 --> 00:15:14.825
[cackles]

00:15:14.908 --> 00:15:16.158
Before you take your leave,

00:15:16.241 --> 00:15:18.533
you need to tell us
everything you know.

00:15:18.616 --> 00:15:20.075
Is that clear, detective?

00:15:20.158 --> 00:15:22.783
Indeed, it was all
initiated on the evening

00:15:22.866 --> 00:15:26.366
of Mask DeMasque's inaugural
infractions of illegality.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.991
As he scampered from
the scene, he stumbled into

00:15:29.075 --> 00:15:32.408
a side street, where nary
a soul stood sentry.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.283
[LUKE] Nary a soul save
the sobriquet Ace Detective,

00:15:38.366 --> 00:15:40.366
surreptitiously
surveying the spot.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:43.533
So it came to pass that
Mask DeMasque would be unmasked.

00:15:43.616 --> 00:15:45.116
At that moment I masterminded

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.366
a magnificent maneuver
for myself in the matter

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:48.908
of the moonlighting marauder.

00:15:48.991 --> 00:15:50.908
The cat-bird seat I'd
acquired, meant I was capable

00:15:50.991 --> 00:15:52.866
of controlling the criminal
and coercing him

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.241
into committing
continued capers.

00:15:55.325 --> 00:15:57.825
Simultaneously shining
the spotlight on the struggle

00:15:57.908 --> 00:16:00.241
surrounding DeMasque
and the Ace Detective.

00:16:00.325 --> 00:16:02.991
Whatever I wanted
was well within warrant!

00:16:03.075 --> 00:16:06.033
I made myself master of
Mask DeMasque and the masses.

00:16:06.116 --> 00:16:08.158
They were practically
pirouetting in my palm.

00:16:08.241 --> 00:16:11.200
And... at the conclusion
I could claim his capture.

00:16:11.283 --> 00:16:13.408
Resulting in reports of
my righteous reputation

00:16:13.491 --> 00:16:15.033
resounding 'round the realm!

00:16:15.116 --> 00:16:18.200
Ah! I'd be atop
the apex of acclamation!

00:16:18.283 --> 00:16:20.700
You were really
doing all this for fame?

00:16:20.783 --> 00:16:22.075
Alas!

00:16:22.158 --> 00:16:24.491
An unanticipated obstruction
unfortunately occurred.

00:16:24.575 --> 00:16:26.700
I can only guess that
Kane Bullard got a whiff of

00:16:26.783 --> 00:16:28.075
the schemes you'd
been percolating?

00:16:28.158 --> 00:16:30.158
--[LUKE growls]
--[SECURITY GUARD] Hold it!

00:16:30.241 --> 00:16:32.241
[LUKE] I summoned my servant
to steal something sacred

00:16:32.325 --> 00:16:34.825
to the CEO of the selfsame
security syndicate.

00:16:34.908 --> 00:16:36.241
This scarlet stone.

00:16:36.325 --> 00:16:38.200
He figured out the
fact that the fancy fixture

00:16:38.283 --> 00:16:39.991
was affixed to my finger.

00:16:40.075 --> 00:16:41.575
Before I knew it,

00:16:41.658 --> 00:16:44.491
I was being blackmailed by that
behemoth blackguard, Bullard.

00:16:44.575 --> 00:16:46.366
Unbelievable!

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:49.950
You mean to tell us
Kane Bullard blackmailed you?

00:16:50.033 --> 00:16:52.116
For his deliberate
display of disrespect,

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.908
I decided that he should die.

00:16:53.991 --> 00:16:55.741
After careful calculation,
it came to me that

00:16:55.825 --> 00:16:58.908
I could co-opt my current
client to carry out this caper.

00:16:58.991 --> 00:17:01.700
Are you saying you used
the Kurain exhibit as cover?

00:17:01.783 --> 00:17:03.283
Yes, precisely!

00:17:03.366 --> 00:17:05.241
It could prove possible
to permanently purge

00:17:05.325 --> 00:17:07.116
the person picking my pocket.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.866
And furthermore frame the
fabled phantom for the felony.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.616
Thus, in the bowels of
that boutique's basement...

00:17:13.408 --> 00:17:15.575
...my magnificently
masterful machinations

00:17:15.658 --> 00:17:18.158
were set into motion!

00:17:18.241 --> 00:17:20.866
You sent the calling
card to Lordly Tailor.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.283
The next step...

00:17:22.366 --> 00:17:24.491
...was to take that staged
photo on the premises

00:17:24.575 --> 00:17:26.491
to shore up an alibi.

00:17:26.575 --> 00:17:28.491
And then you delivered
Bullard's blackmail letter

00:17:28.575 --> 00:17:30.325
to Ron DeLite.

00:17:30.408 --> 00:17:32.616
That's what drew him to
KB Security on the night

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:33.866
of the double crimes.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:35.991
Which brings us to
the last part of the plan.

00:17:36.075 --> 00:17:37.908
To take the fall for the stolen
urn which would mean

00:17:37.991 --> 00:17:39.991
a far less severe penalty.

00:17:40.075 --> 00:17:41.866
Because you thought
you'd be famous?

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:44.741
[LUKE giggles] I'd be lauded
as a living legend

00:17:44.825 --> 00:17:47.075
of both law and larceny!

00:17:47.158 --> 00:17:49.616
The surprise would
secure my celebrity.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.575
Yes. Imagine the shockwaves,
shuttling throughout society!

00:17:53.658 --> 00:17:56.033
An ingenius plan generated
by the most gargantuan

00:17:56.116 --> 00:17:58.908
of geniuses to have
ever graced the globe!

00:17:58.991 --> 00:18:00.075
That's enough!

00:18:00.158 --> 00:18:02.033
[LUKE]
Heh?

00:18:02.116 --> 00:18:05.533
[GODOT] You rode up on a high
octane rocket and flamed out

00:18:05.616 --> 00:18:07.700
in a blaze of glory.

00:18:07.783 --> 00:18:09.700
What's left is dark and empty.

00:18:12.658 --> 00:18:15.575
Thirst can make a man
guzzle down everything there is.

00:18:15.658 --> 00:18:18.283
At this point, brother,
it's all over but the crying.

00:18:18.366 --> 00:18:23.700
[LUKE growls, sobs]

00:18:28.741 --> 00:18:30.366
[JUDGE]
In all my years on the bench,

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.575
the case brought before
this court today is among

00:18:32.658 --> 00:18:35.366
the most complicated that
I have ever encountered

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.908
[JUDGE] But justice has
prevailed in the end.

00:18:37.991 --> 00:18:40.491
This young man narrowly avoided
being labeled a murderer

00:18:40.575 --> 00:18:42.116
and stricken of his freedom.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.741
So it's time this
court hands down

00:18:43.825 --> 00:18:46.575
the verdict he deserves.

00:18:46.658 --> 00:18:47.825
Not Guilty!

00:18:47.908 --> 00:18:50.116
[CROWD cheerin]

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.116
[sighs]

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.991
[BOTH]
Hooray!

00:18:53.075 --> 00:18:55.325
Well done, Phoenix.
I'm proud of you.

00:18:55.408 --> 00:18:58.325
Thank you. I needed your help.

00:18:58.408 --> 00:18:59.908
Promise me this.

00:18:59.991 --> 00:19:01.866
That you'll continue
to watch over Maya.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.200
[gasps]

00:19:07.241 --> 00:19:09.408
Did we win?

00:19:09.491 --> 00:19:12.116
Yes, we did. Thanks to you.

00:19:13.616 --> 00:19:15.866
I appreciate all
your help, Mr. Wright.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.700
You saved my life.

00:19:17.783 --> 00:19:19.533
But... the reality is,
I actually don't have

00:19:19.616 --> 00:19:21.283
all that much to
live for anymore.

00:19:21.366 --> 00:19:22.950
--[PHOENIX] Hmm?
--I know that was stressful,

00:19:23.033 --> 00:19:24.700
but don't be so
down in the dumps.

00:19:24.783 --> 00:19:26.658
You beat a murder rap,
and didn't even get charged

00:19:26.741 --> 00:19:28.533
for whatever you did
as Mask DeMasque.

00:19:28.616 --> 00:19:30.116
Ixnay on Askmay.

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:32.408
I was able to
hold on to my freedom.

00:19:32.491 --> 00:19:34.700
But I feel like it cost
me everything else.

00:19:34.783 --> 00:19:36.033
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:19:36.116 --> 00:19:38.158
All I ever truly wanted
was for my darling Dessie

00:19:38.241 --> 00:19:41.450
to be happy. But this was
the only way that I knew

00:19:41.533 --> 00:19:44.325
how to get enough money to
make sure she stayed that way.

00:19:44.408 --> 00:19:46.158
By being the phantom thief?

00:19:46.241 --> 00:19:47.783
Dessie is pure.

00:19:47.866 --> 00:19:50.908
She's not the type of woman who
would be married to a criminal.

00:19:50.991 --> 00:19:53.450
So I know this means
I'm gonna lose her.

00:19:53.533 --> 00:19:56.408
Now, calm down.
I'm sure she'll forgive you.

00:19:56.491 --> 00:19:59.658
You can't just put a
broken bowl back together again!

00:19:59.741 --> 00:20:01.033
[GROUP]
Hmm?

00:20:01.116 --> 00:20:04.158
[gasps] You got through it,
Ronnie! I'm so happy!

00:20:04.241 --> 00:20:07.658
[RON]
Dessie! That was a close call.

00:20:07.741 --> 00:20:08.825
But, listen...

00:20:08.908 --> 00:20:10.325
[DESIRÉE]
Oh, sweetie.

00:20:10.408 --> 00:20:13.325
Why didn't you ever talk to
me about what was going on?

00:20:13.408 --> 00:20:15.075
I knew you were
into Mask DeMasque,

00:20:15.158 --> 00:20:16.991
but I never thought
you were him.

00:20:17.075 --> 00:20:19.908
I'm sorry, Dessie, I know
you can't stand criminals.

00:20:19.991 --> 00:20:23.866
[gasps] Oh. The only
types of people I can't stand

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.075
are slimy and
full of themselves.

00:20:26.158 --> 00:20:27.866
Like that awful detective.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.575
Wait. Are you saying...?

00:20:29.658 --> 00:20:31.533
But you always gave
fair warning and declared

00:20:31.616 --> 00:20:34.616
your intentions before
sticking it to your targets.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:37.075
It only proves that
you're the guy for me.

00:20:37.158 --> 00:20:39.408
That kind of sportsmanship
turns me on.

00:20:39.491 --> 00:20:41.533
You are talking about crimes.

00:20:41.616 --> 00:20:42.908
You mean that?

00:20:42.991 --> 00:20:46.366
[DESIRÉE]
Hmm. Hey, Nicky boy.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.575
Uh, yes?

00:20:47.658 --> 00:20:49.325
Asking you to defend
my Ronnie was one of

00:20:49.408 --> 00:20:52.741
the best decisions of my life.
Thanks for your hard work.

00:20:52.825 --> 00:20:54.450
Oh, yeah. Sure!

00:20:54.533 --> 00:20:58.533
Aw, look at that. You're
blushing like a little kid.

00:20:58.616 --> 00:21:00.700
You guys did such
a wonderful job in there!

00:21:00.783 --> 00:21:02.491
Major congratulations!

00:21:02.575 --> 00:21:04.200
[gasps]

00:21:04.283 --> 00:21:06.158
Hang on. Let me explain.

00:21:06.241 --> 00:21:08.658
Making time
with another man's wife.

00:21:08.741 --> 00:21:11.533
And right in front of
poor Mystic Maya.

00:21:11.616 --> 00:21:12.991
How dare you!

00:21:13.075 --> 00:21:14.783
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:21:14.866 --> 00:21:16.700
[PHOENIX] As I slipped into
unconsciousness,

00:21:16.783 --> 00:21:19.616
I thought about the
case we just closed.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.991
Ron said that a broken
bowl can never be put back

00:21:22.075 --> 00:21:25.533
together again,
but I know that's not true.

00:21:25.616 --> 00:21:27.783
I offer this urn as exhibit A.

00:21:27.866 --> 00:21:30.366
Back in one piece
and better than before.

00:21:36.533 --> 00:21:38.658
Well, Mister Trite.

00:21:38.741 --> 00:21:41.908
It would appear that the party
has only just begun.

00:21:41.991 --> 00:21:44.533
Let's drink in
everything it has to offer.

00:21:48.033 --> 00:21:49.575
Ah. Bitter.

00:23:20.908 --> 00:23:22.033
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.116 --> 00:23:23.866
We were all kids
when it happened.

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:27.241
A tragic incident that sent
a dear friend far away.

00:23:27.325 --> 00:23:29.491
But a signal from the radio
reminds us of how close

00:23:29.575 --> 00:23:31.075
we really are.

00:23:31.158 --> 00:23:32.825
Little Edgeworth may
feel lost living in

00:23:32.908 --> 00:23:34.825
that cold von Karma household.

00:23:34.908 --> 00:23:38.533
But as we can see, that
which is lost, can be found.

00:23:38.616 --> 00:23:41.325
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:41.408 --> 00:23:43.575
Our next episode
is an anime original:

00:23:43.658 --> 00:23:46.450
"Sound the Turnabout
Melody!" Take that!
